REVERSI - INTERACTIVE 8x8 BLACK vs COM (WHITE)

Use a physical terminal or MCP PTY. Never execute_command reversi.
For MCP: terminal_send({text:"reversi"}), terminal_send({key:"ENTER"}), terminal_read({}),
terminal_send({key:"SPACE"}), terminal_read({}); press q to exit.
Keys: arrows or h/j/k/l move; SPACE places Black; q quits.
B = player, W = COM, . = empty. Latest move: [B] or [W].
The cursor is inverse video. Turn: PLAYER means input is expected.
After a legal move, Turn: COM / COM is thinking... appears and
COM responds about one second later. Sending keys does not wait.
No legal move: automatic pass. Neither can move: game over.
Invalid moves: PLAYER n COM m counts illegal SPACE attempts.
See /man/pty for terminal screen markers and key names.
